      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're pointing out that the debate around suffering, resilience, and hope often elides the ultimate reality: our finite existence. Accepting the limitations and inevitabilities of our lives can indeed be a powerful act of self-assertion, allowing us to reclaim agency and what little control we have over our own mortal trajectory. This perspective can be seen as a radical extension of the traditional human aspiration for self-determination, albeit one that makes explicit the limits of that power.",
